@startuml "Proxy - Pricing (Homework) - Class Diagram"
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<spacer>> transparent
  BorderColor<<spacer>> transparent
  FontColor<<spacer>> transparent
}
hide <<spacer>> stereotype
hide <<spacer>> circle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Proxy — homework 1, the caching proxy


interface PriceService <<Subject>> {
  + priceOf(sku) : Money
}

class SupplierPriceService <<RealSubject>> {
  + calls() : int
}

class CachingPriceProxy <<Proxy>> {
  - cache : Map<String, Entry>
  - ttlMillis : long
  + hits() : int
  + misses() : int
  + invalidate(sku)
}

interface Clock
class ManualClock

PriceService <|.. SupplierPriceService
PriceService <|.. CachingPriceProxy
Clock <|.. ManualClock

note right of CachingPriceProxy
  Five identical requests cost
  <b>one</b> supplier call.

  A decorator forwards and adds.
  This forwards <b>sometimes</b>, and the
  benefit is in the times it does not.
end note

note bottom of Clock
  Injected, so expiry is tested
  without any test sleeping.
end note

note as N1
  The easy half is the saving.
  The hard half is <b>invalidation</b>: for up
  to one TTL this returns a price that is
  wrong, and confidently. No pattern fixes
  that — somebody decides how stale the
  business can afford to be.
end note

class " " as Spacer1 <<spacer>>
PriceService -[hidden]- Spacer1
PriceService -[hidden]- Spacer1
SupplierPriceService -[hidden]right- Spacer1
Spacer1 -[hidden]right- CachingPriceProxy
CachingPriceProxy o-[norank]-> "1" PriceService : supplier
CachingPriceProxy o-[norank]-> "1" Clock
@enduml
